<title>USA: US FCC files new appeal of telecom rule stay.</title>
<headline>US FCC files new appeal of telecom rule stay.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Justice Department, on behalf of the Federal Communications Commission, has filed a new appeal with the U.S. Supreme Court seeking to lift a lower court stay of the FCC's rules designed to open the local phone market to competition.</p>
<p>The action came immediately after Supreme Court Justice Clarence Thomas refused to lift the stay issued earlier this month by a U.S. appeals court in St. Louis.</p>
<p>The latest request was filed with Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg, and she is expected to refer the case to the entire high court for action.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, a coalition of companies led by AT&amp;T Corp and MCI Communications Corp has asked Justice John Paul Stevens to lift the stay.</p>
</text>
